<title>GERMANY: Helaba says 1996 oper profit rises 20.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Helaba says 1996 oper profit rises 20.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    383.9   up 20.6 pct</p>
<p>    Group net profit			    140.4   vs 114.9</p>
<p>    Net interest income			 1,146   vs 894.3</p>
<p>    Net commission income		     123.7   up 0.9 pct</p>
<p>    Net own-account trading income	  19.1    down 79.4 pct</p>
<p>    Fixed investments			   373.2   vs 300.7</p>
<p>    Group balance sheet total		 174,800 vs 157,200</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German publicly-owned regional bank is Helaba Landesbank Hessen-Thueringen AG. All numbers are preliminary, the bank said in a statement. The bank also said it was satisfied with the result, given that it was in a phase requiring heavy investments on technology and building. Business picked up markedly in the second half of the year.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
